From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:06:37 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(export): add 16:9 and 1:1 export profiles

Add youtube_landscape (1920x1080) and square (1080x1080) to
EXPORT_PRESETS. Both use YouTube's 1080p SDR row (8 Mbps at 30 fps or
below, 12 Mbps above, AAC 384 kbps) and fit the whole vertical picture
inside the frame, never stretching or cropping it. The side or top bands
are a blurred, cropped copy of the same clip, so burned-in captions stay
inside the frame with the rest of the picture.

The three existing vertical presets keep their pad filter, geometry and
rates unchanged. New tests cover the table, filters and a real render of
all five profiles.

Attribution: OpenCode (DeepSeek V4.1 Flash Free), lane-b/render-basics.
